<title>ITALY: Bank of Italy sets $4.0 billion repo tender.</title>
<headline>Bank of Italy sets $4.0 billion repo tender.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Italy said it called a $4.0 billion repurchase tender for Friday for government securities to be resold on June 25.</p>
<p>At the previous one-month foreign currency operation for 3.0 billion marks on March 14, the minimum accepted rate stood at 7.33 percent and the average rate at 7.35 percent.</p>
<p>Friday's tender renews a similar amount expiring.</p>
<p>--Milan bureau +39 2 66129507</p>
